{"hash": "d175fbffb1202c93", "text": "The agent types every git command: commits, branches, conflicts, pushes, pull requests, fixes for failing checks. Asked, it lists the files it changed, says whether a remote exists and is public, and names the default branch. You check that a copy elsewhere exists, private or public as you intend; which branch is the default, and which one your host deploys; and the changed files. You decide what merges, and you ask for evidence, not a claim. Saying \"don't push\" makes auto mode block a push, but that can be lost when the conversation is compacted. For a guarantee, use a deny rule or branch protection: the lesson on rules that actually hold. Bring in an expert when shared history must be rewritten; when a secret or personal data was pushed, since the key must be revoked and rotated first: the lesson on keys; or when you can't tell what a step touched on a machine with real credentials.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "a", "g", "e", "n", "t", " ", "t", "y", "p", "e", "s", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "g", "i", "t", " ", "c", "o", "m", "m", "a", "n", "d", ":", " ", "c", "o", "m", "m", "i", "t", "s", ",", " ", "b", "r", "a", "n", "c", "h", "e", "s", ",", " ", "c", "o", "n", "f", "l", "i", "c", "t", "s", ",", " ", "p", "u", "s", "h", "e", "s", ",", " ", "p", "u", "l", "l", " ", "r", "e", "q", "u", "e", "s", "t", "s", ",", " ", "f", "i", "x", "e", "s", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "f", "a", "i", "l", "i", "n", "g", " ", "c", "h", "e", "c", "k", "s", ".", " ", "A", "s", "k", "e", "d", ",", " ", "i", "t", " ", "l", "i", "s", "t", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "i", "l", "e", "s", " ", "i", "t", " ", "c", "h", "a", "n", "g", "e", "d", ",", " ", "s", "a", "y", "s", " ", "w", "h", "e", "t", "h", "e", "r", " ", "a", " ", "r", "e", "m", "o", "t", "e", " ", "e", "x", "i", "s", "t", "s", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "i", "s", " ", "p", "u", "b", "l", "i", "c", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "n", "a", "m", "e", "s", " ", "